// Title: Potential Libvlc.DLL Sideloading
// Sigma ID: bf9808c4-d24f-44a2-8398-b65227d406b6
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: X__Junior
// Date: 2023-04-17 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading of "libvlc.dll", a DLL that is legitimately used by "VLC.exe"
// False positives:
//   - False positives are expected if VLC is installed in non-default locations
// References:
//   - https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/23/c/earth-preta-updated-stealthy-strategies.html
//   - https://hijacklibs.net/entries/3rd_party/vlc/libvlc.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_libvlc.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\libvlc.dll" and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\VideoLAN\\VLC\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\VideoLAN\\VLC\\")))
